A participant should realistically say:

> "I could use some version of this tomorrow."


Q3.1 The proposed list spans too many domains to make every item a priority. How should the Top 10 use it?

A3.1 Rank cross-domain CSA decision loops first; use the list as relevance evidence, not a coverage quota

--
Q3.2 What checkable proxy should replace the subjective statement “I could use some version of this tomorrow”?

A3.2 A CSA can adapt the loop pattern aligned to at least one listed work types in less than a day using existing Copilot access and safe local inputs 

--
Q3.3 Should ranking keep all ten dimensions equal, or emphasize the core teaching objective and immediate role relevance?

A3.3 Double Loop Visibility, Outcome-Based Architecture Potential, Immediate Applicability, and Workshop fit; keep others at 1

--
Q3.4 When should a previously ledgered idea be deliberately revisited rather than excluded as already seen?

A3.4 Only when a changed constraint, new evidence, or materially different loop mechanic creates a named testable hypothesis